  "_files": "What the INSTALLATION provides: the three modules' files. unix_main.c's Sys_LoadDll checks access(fs_basepath/<fs_game>/<name>.mp.i386.so, R_OK) before it dlopens that path, and a real install has the files there (the 2.60b installer unpacks them into etmain/). Their content is never read: the modules are linked into the program and dlopen resolves them by name.",
  "files": {
    "etmain/cgame.mp.i386.so": "PRISM links this module into the program; dlopen finds it by this name (src/env/dl.js).\n",
    "etmain/qagame.mp.i386.so": "PRISM links this module into the program; dlopen finds it by this name (src/env/dl.js).\n",
    "etmain/ui.mp.i386.so": "PRISM links this module into the program; dlopen finds it by this name (src/env/dl.js).\n"
  },
  "_unitDefines": "BOTLIB for botlib/ as SConscript.core's botlib_env adds it. unix/unix_main.c gets __i386__ back for Sys_GetDLLName's '.mp.i386.so' (it #errors on an unknown arch), while every other unit has it off so q_shared.h picks id386 0 and the C paths.",
  "asmTranslate": [
    "src/unix/snapvector.asm",
    {
      "file": "src/unix/snd_mixa.spp",
      "syntax": "gas",
      "defines": {
        "__linux__": "1",
        "__i386__": "1",
        "ELF": "1"
      }
    }
  ],
  "_asmTranslate": "unix/snapvector.asm is Sys_SnapVector in NASM (x87), as Quake III's. unix/snd_mixa.spp is GNU as through cpp, with what SConscript.core's gas_env gives it: ELF, and gcc -m32's __linux__ and __i386__ (its #if id386 needs them; the C units are built without __i386__). It is the only S_WriteLinearBlastStereo16 a Linux build links: snd_mix.c declares it under __linux__, and its C twin is in an #else no Linux configuration reaches. unix/matha.spp is not listed: nothing undefined names its routines.",
  "_dir": "The repository root, not src/: cgame, game and ui include ../../etmain/ui/menudef.h, which lives outside src/ and must be in the tree the page is served."
}
